# Shared skill library — read before changing skills or agent instructions

`/home/julian/dev/weft-fabric` is the **shared** library for Claude Code,
Codex, Gemini/Antigravity and Cursor. There is **one copy of everything** and
every CLI is symlinked to it.

So an edit you make lands in every other agent's context immediately:

- editing `principles/AGENTS.md` changes what Claude, Codex and Gemini load next session
- editing a `SKILL.md` changes the skill the other CLIs run
- deleting a skill removes it from **all** of them at once

There is no per-CLI copy, no staging, no review step.

**Fix outright bugs freely** — a broken path, a dangling symlink, a stale
command. **Adding, retiring, restructuring or re-linking a skill, and any edit
to `principles/AGENTS.md`, is the owner's call** — not a decision to make inside
one session because it looked right from here.

The CLIs also differ in built-ins, so a skill that looks redundant here may be
the only implementation another CLI has. A skill is redundant only if it is
redundant *everywhere*.

Full contract: **`/home/julian/dev/weft-fabric/ARRANGEMENT.md`** — read it
before any of the above.
